noncomputable section

/-! ## (A) The S1 gear's Born self-overlap IS the banked self-blind survival fraction. -/

/-- THE S1 GEAR'S BORN PROBABILITY (self-overlap): defined DIRECTLY as the banked self-blind
    "others" Born-survival fraction `tr Poth / 3` (N308). The S1 gear amplitude `√(2/3)` dissolves
    through the Born SQUARE to this RATIONAL self-overlap (the N306/N311 move) — no ℝ needed. -/
def s1BornProb : ℚ := Matrix.trace Poth / 3

/-- ★ THE S1 SURVIVAL FALLS OUT OF THE BANKED SELF-BLIND FRACTION: `s1BornProb = 2/3`, the Born
    self-overlap of a generation-probe blind to itself on the ℤ₃ cycle (N308 `selfseen_two_thirds`). -/
theorem s1BornProb_value : s1BornProb = 2 / 3 := selfseen_two_thirds

/-! ## (B) THE DECOMPOSITION: the `m_b` Born ratio = (deferred) phase factor × the banked survival. -/

/-- THE `m_b` BORN MASS RATIO (structural): the key's `(tan²P · cosP · √(2/3))²` factored over the
    Born square into `phaseBorn · s1BornProb`, where `phaseBorn = (tan²P · cosP)²` is the fold-PHASE
    Born factor (needs the fold phase `P` = target O3, route-not-yet-found — a DEFERRED free
    parameter, NEVER fit), and `s1BornProb` is the banked self-blind survival. -/
def mbBornRatio (phaseBorn : ℚ) : ℚ := phaseBorn * s1BornProb

/-- ★★ THE S1 GEAR DECOMPOSITION (arc-M M2 headline): the `m_b` Born ratio decomposes EXACTLY into
    the (deferred) fold-phase Born factor times the BANKED self-blind Born-survival `tr Poth / 3`.
    The survival factor is not chosen — it IS the banked N308 self-blind fraction. -/
theorem mbBornRatio_decomp (phaseBorn : ℚ) :
    mbBornRatio phaseBorn = phaseBorn * (Matrix.trace Poth / 3) := by
  rw [mbBornRatio, s1BornProb]

/-- ★ THE DECOMPOSITION AT THE BANKED VALUE: `mbBornRatio phaseBorn = phaseBorn · (2/3)` — the
    survival gear contributes exactly the banked self-blind fraction `2/3` (N308). -/
theorem mbBornRatio_value (phaseBorn : ℚ) :
